e_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1010 emits exactly one outgoing edge in the window (to 66, at t in [68719,70518]); its earlier event does not touch 66. 883 is reached only by three single-shot inbound edges (729, 1038, 1209), one of which precedes 1010's emission entirely. Within the maximal 600-per-hop envelope [68719,72918], 1010's 3-hop time-ignoring cone is only {66,499,1952,1090} and contains neither 883 nor any of its in-neighbours; the shortest static route is five hops (1010-66-1952-1090-729-883), which cannot be packed into the delay budget with correct ordering. The static connection therefore exists only when time is ignored, and the high ambient event volume (5330 events, 1854 nodes) rather than a directed chain accounts for it."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure of the endpoints (step_02, step_03, step_04):** Both nodes are very sparsely active in the window \u2014 1010 has just 2 events with a *single* outgoing partner (node 66), and 883 has 3 events with inbound edges only from {729, 1038, 1209}. So any cascade must start with the unique edge 1010\u219266 and end on one of those three inbound edges (each occurring exactly once, step_10/11/12).\n\n**Timing (step_06, step_13, step_07, step_14):** 1010's outgoing event to 66 is localized to [68719, 70518] (and 1010's other event is earlier, in [56117,63317], where no 1010\u201366 edge exists at all \u2014 step_09, so that earlier event cannot seed the chain). 883's inbound events fall in [63318,66918] (too early to be caused by the 1010\u219266 event) and in [70519,74118].\n\n**Reachability envelope (step_16):** With a 600-unit maximum inter-hop delay, a chain starting at t\u2081 \u2265 68719 can only extend ~600 units per hop. Taking the generous envelope [68719, 72918] (t\u2081 + 4 hops), 1010's entire *time-ignoring* 3-hop neighbourhood is only {66, 499, 1952, 1090} \u2014 883 is absent, and so are all three of 883's in-neighbours.\n\n**Confounder control (step_15):** 883's own 2-hop in-neighbourhood over [68719,74118] is {296, 729, 1090, 1209, 1542}. The only overlap with 1010's forward cone is 1090, which sits at hop 3 from 1010 and hop 2 back from 883 \u2014 i.e. the shortest static path is 1010\u219266\u21921952\u21921090\u2192729\u2192883, five hops. Compressing five hops each \u2264600 units into the residual budget while also respecting the required event ordering (1952 must reach 1090 *before* 1090 reaches 729) is not supported by anything observed; 729 does not even appear in 1010's 3-hop reach for that envelope.\n\n**Volume/popularity control (step_01):** The window holds 5330 events over 1854 nodes with a low repeat ratio (0.028) \u2014 a dense, diffuse background. The endpoints are among the least active nodes in it, so ambient volume, not a directed chain, explains any weak static connectivity.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_ab8543e3\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883, 66, 1952, 1090, 729, 1209, 1038],\n  \"window\": [56117, 84917],\n  \"confidence\": 0.66,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1010 emits exactly one outgoing edge in the window (to 66, at t in [68719,70518]); its earlier event does not touch 66. 883 is reached only by three single-shot inbound edges (729, 1038, 1209), one of which precedes 1010's emission entirely. Within the maximal 600-per-hop envelope [68719,72918], 1010's 3-hop time-ignoring cone is only {66,499,1952,1090} and contains neither 883 nor any of its in-neighbours; the shortest static route is five hops (1010-66-1952-1090-729-883), which cannot be packed into the delay budget with correct ordering. The static connection therefore exists only when time is ignored, and the high ambient event volume (5330 events, 1854 nodes) rather than a directed chain accounts for it.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 45724, "total_output_tokens": 6594, "total_tokens": 52318, "total_latency_ms": 89161, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}